# Calls, Casts, and Requests

This Livebook compares the three public ways to send a Signal to an Agent
Server.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A Counter

```elixir
defmodule RequestGuide.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "request_guide_counter"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/requests"

    route "counter.add" do
      action %{amount: amount},
        name: "request_guide_add",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{amount: Zoi.integer()}),
        context: context do
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | count: context.agent_state.count + amount}}
      end

      define :add, args: [:amount]
    end
  end
end
```

## Start The Actor

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, counter} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    Jido.default_instance(),
    RequestGuide.Counter,
    id: "request-counter"
  )
```

## Call And Wait

```elixir
{:ok, signal} = RequestGuide.Counter.add_signal(2)

{:ok, committed} =
  Jido.AgentServer.call(
    counter,
    signal,
    context: %{request_id: "req-1"},
    timeout: 5_000
  )

committed.state.count
```

`call/3` waits for the commit or failure. Its timeout also defines the admission
deadline. If the caller stops waiting after work starts, the Turn can continue.

## Cast Without A Reply

```elixir
{:ok, cast_signal} = RequestGuide.Counter.add_signal(3)
:ok = Jido.AgentServer.cast(counter, cast_signal)

# A later call from the same process arrives after the cast.
{:ok, barrier_signal} = RequestGuide.Counter.add_signal(0)
{:ok, after_cast} = Jido.AgentServer.call(counter, barrier_signal)

after_cast.state.count
```

A cast is best effort under overload. It does not confirm admission or commit.

## Send Now And Receive Later

```elixir
{:ok, request_signal} = RequestGuide.Counter.add_signal(4)
request_id = Jido.AgentServer.send_request(counter, request_signal)

response = Jido.AgentServer.receive_response(request_id, 5_000)
response
```

The request API lets one process send several requests before it waits. Keep
the request ID in runtime state, not durable Agent state.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(Jido.default_instance(), counter)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Admission, Cancellation, And Timeouts](admission-cancellation-and-timeouts.md)
for failure and wait rules.
